WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.323 --> 00:00:09.164
Imagine a utopian world.

00:00:09.164 --> 00:00:11.622
What does your world look like?

00:00:11.622 --> 00:00:16.714
My world is full of colors;
some colors are indescribable.

00:00:16.714 --> 00:00:20.626
The trees are vibrant and swish 
in the gentle breeze.

00:00:20.626 --> 00:00:24.405
Meadows are full of a variety
of bright flowers.

00:00:24.405 --> 00:00:27.373
Nature flourishes next to bustling cities.

00:00:27.373 --> 00:00:31.805
People are agreeable to one another
and are open to different perspectives.

00:00:31.805 --> 00:00:35.915
My world lacks ignorance and overflows
with compassion and understanding

00:00:35.915 --> 00:00:37.545
for one another.

00:00:37.545 --> 00:00:40.196
It is fueled by love.

00:00:40.196 --> 00:00:43.096
My world is fueled by a love of nature,

00:00:43.096 --> 00:00:44.066
a love of knowledge,

00:00:44.066 --> 00:00:45.285
a love of empathy,

00:00:45.285 --> 00:00:47.165
a love for one another,
and most of all,

00:00:47.165 --> 00:00:50.535
a love for our future, our children.

00:00:50.535 --> 00:00:56.815
My world is a world where every child is
born with potential and equal opportunity.

00:00:56.815 --> 00:01:00.086
Children are the future
and governments realize this.

00:01:00.086 --> 00:01:04.816
They invest more into the success and
education of the future.

00:01:04.816 --> 00:01:08.617
It is not a world ripe with violence 
or greed,

00:01:08.617 --> 00:01:10.868
but one of peace and kindness.

00:01:10.868 --> 00:01:15.169
And it most definitely is a world
where each and every child on this screen

00:01:15.169 --> 00:01:20.587
have no obstacles pertaining to their
racial and/or ethnic backgrounds.

00:01:20.587 --> 00:01:26.008
While some of the attributes of my utopian
world are seemingly unattainable,

00:01:26.008 --> 00:01:29.098
others should make us wonder.

00:01:29.098 --> 00:01:33.358
Why is it that the idea of every child
being born with potential

00:01:33.358 --> 00:01:39.418
and equal opportunity
only one of a dream world?

00:01:39.418 --> 00:01:43.168
"What?" you may ask, "Isn't that already
something of the present?

00:01:43.168 --> 00:01:48.808
We all have the same amount
of opportunity at birth, right?"

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:52.629
No. They do not.

00:01:52.629 --> 00:01:54.689
We have a problem.

00:01:54.689 --> 00:01:58.009
Racial judgments 
are ruining children's lives.

00:01:58.009 --> 00:02:05.131
For simplicity, let's define racial judgments 
as judgments related to race and ethnicity.

00:02:05.131 --> 00:02:08.201
We live in a world where a child's future
is almost set in stone

00:02:08.201 --> 00:02:09.940
the moment that they are conceived,

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:14.321
a future that is primarily dependent
on ethnicity.

00:02:14.321 --> 00:02:17.489
Our carelessness and our lack
of awareness when making judgments

00:02:17.489 --> 00:02:21.561
is destructive to our children, 
our future.

00:02:21.561 --> 00:02:27.682
Yes, we have a huge problem,
but we also have a great solution.

00:02:27.682 --> 00:02:30.861
Take a look at the group of children
projected on the screen.

00:02:30.861 --> 00:02:32.120
What do you see?

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:35.954
Do you see a diverse group
of children eagerly waiting to answer?

00:02:35.954 --> 00:02:38.591
We have all determined
that these children are adorable.

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:40.172
How old do they look?

00:02:40.172 --> 00:02:41.712
They seem to be in preschool,

00:02:41.712 --> 00:02:44.553
or more likely kindergarten
or first grade.

00:02:44.553 --> 00:02:47.752
Do you see anything else in this picture?

00:02:47.752 --> 00:02:49.843
Anything else at all?

00:02:49.843 --> 00:02:52.172
Have you made all your observations?

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:57.532
Here are a few observations
that most of you probably didn't make.

00:02:57.532 --> 00:03:00.263
Let's consider a hypothetical situation.

00:03:00.263 --> 00:03:03.153
This is more or less your typical
preschool claass.

00:03:03.153 --> 00:03:07.313
So, let's say that James, 
the white boy in the first row,

00:03:07.313 --> 00:03:11.734
bites Lily's hand, the Japanese
girl to his right of him,

00:03:11.734 --> 00:03:13.724
because she wouldn't give him her crayon.

00:03:13.724 --> 00:03:17.175
On average, the worst punishment
James will get

00:03:17.175 --> 00:03:19.857
is a phone call home and a time out.

00:03:19.857 --> 00:03:21.449
Fair enough, right?

00:03:21.449 --> 00:03:27.798
Ok, same situation, but let's have
Daniel bite Lily's hand.

00:03:27.798 --> 00:03:33.147
Daniel is more likely to be suspended,
if not expelled.

00:03:33.147 --> 00:03:37.890
In fact, black males are three times
more likely to be suspended

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:41.098
than their white counterparts
for the same misbehavior,

00:03:41.098 --> 00:03:43.420
a trend that holds for preschool

00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:47.168
as well as the rest of their
educational careers.

00:03:47.168 --> 00:03:50.385
The idea of black males being
persecuted far more severely

00:03:50.385 --> 00:03:52.047
than their white counterparts

00:03:52.047 --> 00:03:55.156
is prevalent throughout the child's life.

00:03:55.156 --> 00:03:58.519
An example of this is seen in the
school-to-prison pipeline,

00:03:58.519 --> 00:04:02.417
which states that male African Americans
are more likely to go to prison

00:04:02.417 --> 00:04:04.507
straight from school.

00:04:04.507 --> 00:04:09.618
While the situation above is hypothetical,
it is based off of a real-life incident.

00:04:09.618 --> 00:04:13.817
These racial judgments start
in the very beginning, preschool.

00:04:13.817 --> 00:04:18.008
The black girl in the picture, Katie,
is facing consequences just as extreme,

00:04:18.008 --> 00:04:19.808
if not more extreme.

00:04:19.808 --> 00:04:23.128
According to a study conducted by 
Columbia University law professor

00:04:23.128 --> 00:04:25.087
Kimberle Williams Crenshaw,

00:04:25.087 --> 00:04:29.697
black girls and other girls of color
are facing a grave danger.

00:04:29.697 --> 00:04:33.198
While black boys are only three times
more likely to be suspended,

00:04:33.198 --> 00:04:37.480
black girls are six times more prone
to suspension

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:39.728
than their white female classmates.

00:04:39.728 --> 00:04:43.148
In a Baltimore school, a school security
officer claimed to be attacked

00:04:43.148 --> 00:04:45.468
by three black girls.

00:04:45.468 --> 00:04:49.809
The school immediately believed
the officer and expelled the three girls.

00:04:49.809 --> 00:04:52.170
However, after reviewing a security tape,

00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:55.269
it was shown that the officer had
repeatedly hit one of the girls

00:04:55.269 --> 00:04:58.681
on the head with her baton
and pepper sprayed the other girls,

00:04:58.681 --> 00:05:03.520
forcing all three girls to seek treatment
at a hospital.

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:05.210
Why is that?

00:05:05.210 --> 00:05:08.750
Why are these girls in more danger
than white girls?

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:12.460
Well, the study goes on to explain
that black girls and other girls of color

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:15.030
are seen as disruptive and ignorant.

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:19.050
Their achievements are ignored
and their actions are misinterpreted.

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:23.941
Like, for instance, the study claims
that the majority of its participants

00:05:23.941 --> 00:05:26.631
believed that their teachers
viewed them negatively

00:05:26.631 --> 00:05:28.591
and often berated them for being defiant

00:05:28.591 --> 00:05:31.751
when, in fact, 
they were just being curious.

00:05:31.751 --> 00:05:36.043
Furthermore, the girls of color
are facing an intersectional burden

00:05:36.043 --> 00:05:39.471
since their darker skin is associated
with aggressive behavior,

00:05:39.471 --> 00:05:40.671
and as women,

00:05:40.671 --> 00:05:44.351
they have the additional burden 
of being seen as bossy and demanding

00:05:44.351 --> 00:05:46.261
when they are being assertive.

00:05:46.261 --> 00:05:49.242
Thus the discrimination that girls
of color face

00:05:49.242 --> 00:05:52.274
can be far more onerous than that
of boys of color

00:05:52.274 --> 00:05:54.733
because of the difference in gender.

00:05:54.733 --> 00:05:58.973
Racial judgments are ruining
children's lives.

00:05:58.973 --> 00:06:02.334
Not only black children,
other children as well.

00:06:02.334 --> 00:06:04.184
When we see an Asian person,

00:06:04.184 --> 00:06:06.954
we immediately assume
they must be super smart.

00:06:06.954 --> 00:06:10.623
That being said, white people also
have to deal with racial judgments.

00:06:10.623 --> 00:06:16.372
They are typically taken as more racist
and more judgmental than any other race.

00:06:16.372 --> 00:06:19.914
Consider this picture of teens
from different ethnic backgrounds

00:06:19.914 --> 00:06:23.485
speaking out against the racial judgments
they combat.

00:06:23.485 --> 00:06:26.683
These judgments are based off of
stereotypes,

00:06:26.683 --> 00:06:29.752
and these generalizations 
have become jokes.

00:06:29.752 --> 00:06:35.405
We have forgotten that our words
can actually do damage.

00:06:35.405 --> 00:06:38.881
Let's not forget the racial judgments
concerning religion.

00:06:38.881 --> 00:06:41.015
The Pew Research Center conducted
a survey

00:06:41.015 --> 00:06:46.275
where they asked Americans to rate
how warmly they felt about Muslims

00:06:46.275 --> 00:06:50.045
on a thermometer scale
from 0 degrees to 100 degrees.

00:06:50.045 --> 00:06:54.186
The average temperature was 40 degrees,

00:06:54.186 --> 00:06:57.767
significantly cooler than that of 
the rest of the seven religious groups

00:06:57.767 --> 00:06:59.886
that were also surveyed.

00:06:59.886 --> 00:07:03.336
This is because, one, they base their
judgment off of a small percentage

00:07:03.336 --> 00:07:05.006
of extremist Muslims,

00:07:05.006 --> 00:07:08.907
and two, they're ignorant to what
the religion actually stands for.

00:07:08.907 --> 00:07:13.207
This is a problem I myself face
as a young Muslim woman.

00:07:13.207 --> 00:07:17.817
Racial judgments are the reason why I,
a sixteen-year-old girl,

00:07:17.817 --> 00:07:20.490
am pulled aside during airport security.

00:07:20.490 --> 00:07:24.967
While I understand that it's for
my own safety,

00:07:24.967 --> 00:07:29.747
it is tiring and concerning that the
people around me

00:07:29.747 --> 00:07:33.028
may be afraid of me or hate me

00:07:33.028 --> 00:07:36.781
because of a piece of clothing,
my hijab, on my head.

00:07:36.781 --> 00:07:40.360
These types of racial judgments will
surely affect Aaliyah,

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:44.008
the Indian Muslim girl in the back row.

00:07:44.008 --> 00:07:48.279
I, like the majority of Muslims, 
as well as the majority of the world,

00:07:48.279 --> 00:07:51.300
absolutely abhor terrorists.

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:54.849
In every group of people, there is always
going to be a small percentage

00:07:54.849 --> 00:07:59.540
of people who are so extreme that
the larger group must disown them.

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:02.921
But no matter how we try to
separate ourselves from these criminals,

00:08:02.921 --> 00:08:06.700
our physical similarities are too much
for people to overcome.

00:08:06.700 --> 00:08:09.361
Simply because we share 
the same color of skin

00:08:09.361 --> 00:08:11.701
or piece of clothing 
with these terrorists,

00:08:11.701 --> 00:08:14.891
we become targets 
of the same racial judgments.

00:08:14.891 --> 00:08:21.951
In our nation, many of us hold ideals
that race shouldn't matter,

00:08:21.951 --> 00:08:25.232
that most of us have overcome almost
all racial barriers

00:08:25.232 --> 00:08:27.991
and problems caused by race.

00:08:27.991 --> 00:08:30.613
Our statement is a half truth.

00:08:30.613 --> 00:08:34.072
It is true that most of us have overcome
racial barriers

00:08:34.072 --> 00:08:37.052
concerning friendship 
and other aspects of life.

00:08:37.052 --> 00:08:42.442
However, there are still so many aspects
of our lives where race, unfortunately,

00:08:42.442 --> 00:08:44.502
still matters.

00:08:44.502 --> 00:08:47.632
In many cases, our racial backgrounds
determine the level

00:08:47.632 --> 00:08:49.562
of educational opportunity we have,

00:08:49.562 --> 00:08:51.693
the types of lives we will lead,

00:08:51.693 --> 00:08:55.527
and the way we are perceived by society.

00:08:55.527 --> 00:08:59.083
We shouldn't always ignore race.

00:08:59.083 --> 00:09:02.154
Sometimes, knowing a 
person's beliefs or race

00:09:02.154 --> 00:09:04.845
can help you become more respectful
towards that person.

00:09:04.845 --> 00:09:07.543
It can broaden your horizons
and help you form judgments

00:09:07.543 --> 00:09:10.354
that aren't biased and/or ignorant.

00:09:10.354 --> 00:09:14.194
We can't stop racial judgments
or judgments all altogether.

00:09:14.194 --> 00:09:17.935
Judging is an evolutionary trait,
something we needed for our survival.

00:09:17.935 --> 00:09:20.626
Simple judgments, like knowing
when to cross the street,

00:09:20.626 --> 00:09:23.075
or knowing not to go into
a dark alleyway at night,

00:09:23.075 --> 00:09:24.685
are essential for human life,

00:09:24.685 --> 00:09:29.016
which is why stopping racial judgments
is nearly impossible

00:09:29.016 --> 00:09:31.146
and detrimental to our species.

00:09:31.146 --> 00:09:33.816
Here's what we can do.

00:09:33.816 --> 00:09:37.026
We can become aware 
of our racial judgements

00:09:37.026 --> 00:09:40.307
Our awareness will make us think
twice about our judgments.

00:09:40.307 --> 00:09:44.136
It is proven that actively looking
for biases in your racial judgments

00:09:44.136 --> 00:09:47.466
will make your judgments more accurate
and respectful.

00:09:47.466 --> 00:09:51.427
This is because racial judgments
are products of implicit bias,

00:09:51.427 --> 00:09:57.907
a bias in assumptions and behavior
that occur on a subconscious level.

00:09:57.907 --> 00:10:00.237
It is due to the assumptions
and stereotypes

00:10:00.237 --> 00:10:04.947
that we are exposed to 
in our respective environments.

00:10:04.947 --> 00:10:09.656
Implicit bias is automatic,
but it's not intransigent.

00:10:09.656 --> 00:10:11.719
Awareness is the key.

00:10:11.719 --> 00:10:15.128
Next time we find ourselves making
an assumption about someone,

00:10:15.128 --> 00:10:19.958
we need to ask ourselves, why?

00:10:19.958 --> 00:10:22.358
Do we have a good reason?

00:10:22.358 --> 00:10:25.197
Would we be able to justify 
our assumption

00:10:25.197 --> 00:10:28.130
to someone with a different perspective?

00:10:28.130 --> 00:10:31.838
When we ask ourselves these questions,
we tend to second-guess ourselves,

00:10:31.838 --> 00:10:34.948
and in this case, this is a good thing.

00:10:34.948 --> 00:10:36.530
If we second-guess ourselves,

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:39.109
our racial judgments will become
more accurate,

00:10:39.109 --> 00:10:40.399
more respectful,

00:10:40.399 --> 00:10:42.390
and less biased.

00:10:42.390 --> 00:10:44.650
I'm not saying this will be easy.

00:10:44.650 --> 00:10:46.170
It's hard.

00:10:46.170 --> 00:10:51.460
I'm ashamed to admit that I have succumbed
to biased racial judgments.

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:53.731
I've walked down the street
with my best friend

00:10:53.731 --> 00:10:57.051
and we have deliberately changed our pace
or route to avoid

00:10:57.051 --> 00:11:00.951
and African American or white man
in baggy clothing.

00:11:00.951 --> 00:11:04.720
But I think we're taking the first step
in making better racial judgments

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:08.372
when we realize that some of our
judgments are biased.

00:11:08.372 --> 00:11:11.301
I've often found myself judging someone
without realizing

00:11:11.301 --> 00:11:15.523
and then mentally berating 
myself right after.

00:11:15.523 --> 00:11:18.361
So become more aware.

00:11:18.361 --> 00:11:22.373
Ask yourselves the reasons behind your
judgments and assumptions.

00:11:22.373 --> 00:11:27.082
This will help you become more aware
of your judgments and of your thoughts.

00:11:27.082 --> 00:11:29.004
If not for your own sake,

00:11:29.004 --> 00:11:31.203
for the sake of those little preschoolers,

00:11:31.203 --> 00:11:33.744
for the sake of our world's future.

00:11:33.744 --> 00:11:36.154
This awareness will brighten our world,

00:11:36.154 --> 00:11:39.803
creating a safe space for all of our
children to thrive and achieve

00:11:39.803 --> 00:11:41.833
their hopes and dreams.

00:11:41.833 --> 00:11:44.674
And someday, my utopian world,

00:11:44.674 --> 00:11:46.794
our utopian world,

00:11:46.794 --> 00:11:48.445
will become a reality.

00:11:48.445 --> 00:11:49.633
Thank you.

